546-Required constraints:
547-- maintain stop conditions
548-- avoid useless loops
549:- do not discard relevant evidence without reason
550-- do not over-decompose simple questions
551-- keep iterative retrieval tied to improved answer quality
552-- rank follow-up retrieval moves by expected information gain, not by query count
553-- track whether each iteration materially increases `Evidence Coverage`
554:- treat weak provenance, stale indexing, poor chunking, or ambiguous metadata as evidence-surface defects
555:- if repeated judged checkpoints change retrieval mode or stopping threshold, preserve a compact quality iteration checkpoint rather than replaying the whole retrieval path
556:- if the evidence substrate is weak, lower claim strength, narrow scope, or surface `Limitation`
557:- if evidence quality depends on the surrounding briefing or context packaging, preserve a `Context sufficiency review memo` rather than blaming retrieval quality alone
558:- distinguish evidence sufficiency from context sufficiency when stale context, missing user state, or missing task framing could change the answer
